Chapter: Sid

 The MOS 6581/8580 SID: three independent voices, each with a 24-bit
 phase-accumulator oscillator (sawtooth, triangle, variable-width pulse,
 and a 23-bit LFSR noise source), an ADSR envelope, ring modulation and
 hard sync between adjacent voices, a master volume, and the chip's
 resonant multimode filter. The three voices are summed, optionally
 routed through the filter, scaled by the master volume, clamped, and
 written as 48 kHz 16-bit signed stereo PCM -- the format codex-vm's HDA
 output expects (Kernel chapter HdaAudio). A caller renders a buffer with
 sid-render and either reads it back (the silent frequency test) or hands
 it to hda-play-pcm to be heard.

 The three voices are rendered together, one output sample at a time,
 because ring modulation and hard sync couple a voice to its neighbour:
 voice 0 is modulated by voice 2, voice 1 by voice 0, voice 2 by voice 1.
 All per-voice runtime state -- phase accumulator, packed envelope, noise
 LFSR -- plus the two filter integrators live in a 44-byte state block
 (sid-rt), threaded through the sample loop by mutation. sid-render
 allocates and resets a fresh block for a self-contained one-shot tone;
 sid-render-stream takes a caller-owned block so an emulator can keep the
 oscillators and envelopes running continuously across frame boundaries.

 Combined waveforms are approximated by the bitwise AND the chip roughly
 performs. The envelope rates are derived from the published SID rate
 table but quantised to whole output samples rather than the chip's
 15-bit prescaler, so a rate is accurate to within one 48 kHz sample. The
 filter is a fixed-point state-variable (Chamberlin) filter: its cutoff
 and resonance map the 11-bit FC and 4-bit RES registers onto stable
 coefficients rather than reproducing the 6581's exact analogue curve.

 We say:

Section: Constants

  sid-clk : Integer = 985248
  sid-sample-rate : Integer = 48000
  sid-clocks-per-sample : Integer = 20

Section: State Block Layout

 sid-rt is 44 bytes of persistent runtime state, read and written as
 eleven 32-bit slots: voice phase accumulators at 0/4/8, packed envelopes
 at 12/16/20, noise LFSRs at 24/28/32, and the filter's low and band
 integrators (signed) at 36/40. sid-rt-reset seeds a fresh block: phases
 and envelopes and filter zeroed, each noise LFSR seeded non-zero (a zero
 LFSR is stuck at zero).

  sid-rt-reset : Integer -> Integer
  sid-rt-reset (rt) =
    let a0 = poke-32 rt 0 0
    in let a1 = poke-32 rt 4 0
    in let a2 = poke-32 rt 8 0
    in let e0 = poke-32 rt 12 0
    in let e1 = poke-32 rt 16 0
    in let e2 = poke-32 rt 20 0
    in let n0 = poke-32 rt 24 12345
    in let n1 = poke-32 rt 28 12345
    in let n2 = poke-32 rt 32 12345
    in let f0 = poke-32 rt 36 0
    in let f1 = poke-32 rt 40 0
    in a0 + a1 + a2 + e0 + e1 + e2 + n0 + n1 + n2 + f0 + f1

  sid-peek-s32 : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  sid-peek-s32 (base) (off) =
    let raw = peek-32 base off
    in if raw >= #80000000 then raw - #100000000 else raw

Section: Envelope Rate Table

 One envelope step takes this many SID clocks for the attack phase, per
 the 4-bit rate value. Decay and release use the same table times three.

  sid-rate-period : Integer -> Integer
  sid-rate-period (r) =
    when bit-and r 15
      is 0 -> 9
      is 1 -> 32
      is 2 -> 63
      is 3 -> 95
      is 4 -> 149
      is 5 -> 220
      is 6 -> 267
      is 7 -> 313
      is 8 -> 392
      is 9 -> 977
      is 10 -> 1954
      is 11 -> 3126
      is 12 -> 3907
      is 13 -> 11720
      is 14 -> 19532
      is 15 -> 31251
      is otherwise -> 9

Section: Oscillator

 Waveform value in 0..4095 from the 24-bit phase, the control byte's
 waveform bits (triangle #10, sawtooth #20, pulse #40, noise #80), the
 12-bit pulse width, the current noise LFSR, and a ring-modulation bit.
 Selected waveforms are combined by AND; no waveform bit selected is
 silence. Ring modulation replaces the triangle's fold sign (the phase's
 top bit) with that bit XOR the modulator voice's top bit, so a voice
 with the ring bit set folds under the control of its neighbour.

  sid-waveform : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  sid-waveform (phase) (control) (pw) (noise) (modmsb) =
    let tri-on = bit-and control #10
    in let saw-on = bit-and control #20
    in let pul-on = bit-and control #40
    in let nz-on = bit-and control #80
    in if tri-on + saw-on + pul-on + nz-on == 0 then 0
    else
      let saw = bit-shru phase 12
      in let foldbit = bit-xor (bit-and (bit-shru phase 23) 1) modmsb
      in let folded = if foldbit /= 0
        then bit-xor (bit-shru phase 11) #FFFFFF
        else bit-shru phase 11
      in let tri = bit-and folded #FFF
      in let pul = if bit-shru phase 12 >= pw then #FFF else 0
      in let nz = bit-and (bit-shru noise 4) #FFF
      in let a1 = if tri-on /= 0 then bit-and #FFF tri else #FFF
      in let a2 = if saw-on /= 0 then bit-and a1 saw else a1
      in let a3 = if pul-on /= 0 then bit-and a2 pul else a2
      in let a4 = if nz-on /= 0 then bit-and a3 nz else a3
      in a4

  sid-noise-step : Integer -> Integer
  sid-noise-step (n) =
    let tap = bit-and (bit-xor (bit-shru n 22) (bit-shru n 17)) 1
    in bit-and (bit-or (bit-shl n 1) tap) #7FFFFF

 Advance one oscillator by pinc, returning the new 24-bit phase in the
 low bits with an overflow flag (the oscillator wrapped this sample) in
 bit 24. Hard sync watches this flag on the modulator voice.

  sid-osc-advance : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  sid-osc-advance (phase) (pinc) =
    let raw = phase + pinc
    in if raw >= #1000000 then (bit-and raw #FFFFFF) + #1000000
       else raw

Section: Envelope

 The envelope value (0..255), its ADSR state (0 = off/release, 1 =
 attack, 2 = decay-sustain), and its rate counter are packed into one
 integer: env in the low byte, state at *256, rate counter at *1024.

  sid-env-advance : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  sid-env-advance (env) (state) (ratectr) (gate) (att) (dec) (sus) (rel) =
    let st = if gate == 0 then 0 else if state == 0 then 1 else state
    in let rate = if st == 1 then att else if st == 2 then dec else rel
    in let period = if st == 1 then sid-rate-period rate else sid-rate-period rate * 3
    in let sps = let p = period / sid-clocks-per-sample in if p < 1 then 1 else p
    in let rc1 = ratectr + 1
    in if rc1 < sps then env + st * 256 + rc1 * 1024
    else
      let target = if st == 1 then 255 else if st == 2 then sus * 17 else 0
      in let env1 = if env < target then env + 1 else if env > target then env - 1 else env
      in let st1 = if st == 1 then (if env1 >= 255 then 2 else 1) else st
      in env1 + st1 * 256

Section: Sample

 Render one output sample. The three oscillators advance together so
 that hard sync and ring modulation can read each other's phase, then
 each voice's waveform is scaled by its envelope, the routed voices are
 summed into the state-variable filter, and the filtered and unfiltered
 sums are scaled by the master volume, clamped, and written as one
 16-bit stereo frame. Every mutation lands in the sid-rt state block, so
 the next sample resumes exactly where this one left off.

  sid-sample : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  sid-sample (regbase) (rt) (buf) (i) =
    let c0 = peek-byte regbase 4
    in let c1 = peek-byte regbase 11
    in let c2 = peek-byte regbase 18
    in let f0 = peek-byte regbase 0 + peek-byte regbase 1 * 256
    in let f1 = peek-byte regbase 7 + peek-byte regbase 8 * 256
    in let f2 = peek-byte regbase 14 + peek-byte regbase 15 * 256
    in let pinc0 = f0 * sid-clk / sid-sample-rate
    in let pinc1 = f1 * sid-clk / sid-sample-rate
    in let pinc2 = f2 * sid-clk / sid-sample-rate
    in let pk0 = sid-osc-advance (peek-32 rt 0) pinc0
    in let pk1 = sid-osc-advance (peek-32 rt 4) pinc1
    in let pk2 = sid-osc-advance (peek-32 rt 8) pinc2
    in let np0 = bit-and pk0 #FFFFFF
    in let np1 = bit-and pk1 #FFFFFF
    in let np2 = bit-and pk2 #FFFFFF
    in let w0 = bit-shru pk0 24
    in let w1 = bit-shru pk1 24
    in let w2 = bit-shru pk2 24
    in let fp0 = if bit-and c0 2 /= 0 then (if w2 /= 0 then 0 else np0) else np0
    in let fp1 = if bit-and c1 2 /= 0 then (if w0 /= 0 then 0 else np1) else np1
    in let fp2 = if bit-and c2 2 /= 0 then (if w1 /= 0 then 0 else np2) else np2
    in let rm0 = if bit-and c0 4 /= 0 then bit-and (bit-shru np2 23) 1 else 0
    in let rm1 = if bit-and c1 4 /= 0 then bit-and (bit-shru np0 23) 1 else 0
    in let rm2 = if bit-and c2 4 /= 0 then bit-and (bit-shru np1 23) 1 else 0
    in let pw0 = peek-byte regbase 2 + bit-and (peek-byte regbase 3) #F * 256
    in let pw1 = peek-byte regbase 9 + bit-and (peek-byte regbase 10) #F * 256
    in let pw2 = peek-byte regbase 16 + bit-and (peek-byte regbase 17) #F * 256
    in let nz0 = sid-noise-step (peek-32 rt 24)
    in let nz1 = sid-noise-step (peek-32 rt 28)
    in let nz2 = sid-noise-step (peek-32 rt 32)
    in let wv0 = sid-waveform fp0 c0 pw0 nz0 rm0
    in let wv1 = sid-waveform fp1 c1 pw1 nz1 rm1
    in let wv2 = sid-waveform fp2 c2 pw2 nz2 rm2
    in let ep0 = peek-32 rt 12
    in let ep1 = peek-32 rt 16
    in let ep2 = peek-32 rt 20
    in let ne0 = sid-env-advance (int-mod ep0 256) (int-mod (ep0 / 256) 4) (ep0 / 1024) (bit-and c0 1) (bit-shru (peek-byte regbase 5) 4) (bit-and (peek-byte regbase 5) #F) (bit-shru (peek-byte regbase 6) 4) (bit-and (peek-byte regbase 6) #F)
    in let ne1 = sid-env-advance (int-mod ep1 256) (int-mod (ep1 / 256) 4) (ep1 / 1024) (bit-and c1 1) (bit-shru (peek-byte regbase 12) 4) (bit-and (peek-byte regbase 12) #F) (bit-shru (peek-byte regbase 13) 4) (bit-and (peek-byte regbase 13) #F)
    in let ne2 = sid-env-advance (int-mod ep2 256) (int-mod (ep2 / 256) 4) (ep2 / 1024) (bit-and c2 1) (bit-shru (peek-byte regbase 19) 4) (bit-and (peek-byte regbase 19) #F) (bit-shru (peek-byte regbase 20) 4) (bit-and (peek-byte regbase 20) #F)
    in let env0 = int-mod ne0 256
    in let env1 = int-mod ne1 256
    in let env2 = int-mod ne2 256
    in let vo0 = (wv0 - 2048) * 8 * env0 / 256
    in let vo1 = (wv1 - 2048) * 8 * env1 / 256
    in let vo2 = (wv2 - 2048) * 8 * env2 / 256
    in let resreg = peek-byte regbase 23
    in let modereg = peek-byte regbase 24
    in let threeoff = bit-and modereg #80
    in let dry0 = if bit-and resreg 1 /= 0 then 0 else vo0
    in let dry1 = if bit-and resreg 2 /= 0 then 0 else vo1
    in let dry2 = if bit-and resreg 4 /= 0 then 0 else (if threeoff /= 0 then 0 else vo2)
    in let dry = dry0 + dry1 + dry2
    in let fin0 = if bit-and resreg 1 /= 0 then vo0 else 0
    in let fin1 = if bit-and resreg 2 /= 0 then vo1 else 0
    in let fin2 = if bit-and resreg 4 /= 0 then vo2 else 0
    in let fin = fin0 + fin1 + fin2
    in let cutoff = (bit-and (peek-byte regbase 21) 7) + (bit-shl (peek-byte regbase 22) 3)
    in let fc0 = 4 + cutoff * 196 / 2047
    in let fc = if fc0 > 200 then 200 else fc0
    in let res = bit-shru resreg 4
    in let dmp = 256 - res * 12
    in let flow = sid-peek-s32 rt 36
    in let fband = sid-peek-s32 rt 40
    in let fhigh = fin - flow - dmp * fband / 256
    in let nband = fband + fc * fhigh / 256
    in let nlow = flow + fc * nband / 256
    in let flp = if bit-and modereg #10 /= 0 then nlow else 0
    in let fbp = if bit-and modereg #20 /= 0 then nband else 0
    in let fhp = if bit-and modereg #40 /= 0 then fhigh else 0
    in let fout = flp + fbp + fhp
    in let total = dry + fout
    in let master = bit-and modereg #F
    in let scaled = total * master / 15
    in let cl = if scaled > 32767 then 32767 else if scaled < (0 - 32768) then (0 - 32768) else scaled
    in let s = bit-and cl #FFFF
    in let lo = bit-and s #FF
    in let hi = bit-and (bit-shru s 8) #FF
    in let b0 = poke-byte buf (i * 4) lo
    in let b1 = poke-byte buf (i * 4 + 1) hi
    in let b2 = poke-byte buf (i * 4 + 2) lo
    in let b3 = poke-byte buf (i * 4 + 3) hi
    in let s0 = poke-32 rt 0 fp0
    in let s1 = poke-32 rt 4 fp1
    in let s2 = poke-32 rt 8 fp2
    in let se0 = poke-32 rt 12 ne0
    in let se1 = poke-32 rt 16 ne1
    in let se2 = poke-32 rt 20 ne2
    in let sn0 = poke-32 rt 24 nz0
    in let sn1 = poke-32 rt 28 nz1
    in let sn2 = poke-32 rt 32 nz2
    in let sf0 = poke-32 rt 36 nlow
    in let sf1 = poke-32 rt 40 nband
    in 0

Section: Render

 Render nsamples of 48 kHz 16-bit stereo PCM from the 32 SID register
 bytes at regbase into buf (which must hold nsamples * 4 bytes).
 sid-render is a self-contained one-shot: it allocates and resets a fresh
 state block, so each call starts silent. sid-render-stream renders into
 a caller-owned state block and leaves it running, so successive calls
 continue the same oscillators, envelopes and filter without a click.

  sid-loop : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  sid-loop (regbase) (rt) (buf) (nsamples) (i) =
    if i >= nsamples then 0
    else
      let d = sid-sample regbase rt buf i
      in sid-loop regbase rt buf nsamples (i + 1)

  sid-render-stream : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  sid-render-stream (regbase) (rt) (buf) (nsamples) =
    sid-loop regbase rt buf nsamples 0

  sid-render : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  sid-render (regbase) (buf) (nsamples) =
    let rt = alloc-bytes 64
    in let z = sid-rt-reset rt
    in sid-loop regbase rt buf nsamples 0
